Overall Exam Structure & Duration

• Total Duration: 190 minutes
• Parts: Divided into Part A (Foundation) and Part B (Advanced)
• Negative Marking: None

1. Part A: Foundation Section Cut-offs

To clear the Foundation section, you need a minimum total of 45 questions correct out of 65, split across the following sections:
• Numerical Ability (Aptitude): 14 questions correct (out of 20)
• Verbal Ability (English): 18 questions correct (out of 25)
• Reasoning Ability (Logical Reasoning): 14 questions correct (out of 20)

2. Part B: Advanced Section Track-Wise Cut-offs

Your final role allocation (Ninja, Digital, or Prime) is strictly determined by how many questions you solve in the Advanced tier:

Advanced Sub-Section	Ninja Cut-off	Digital Cut-off	Prime Cut-off
Advanced Quant & Reasoning (14 Questions)	0	9 Questions	12 Questions
Advanced Coding (2 Questions)	0	1 Coding Problem	2 Coding Problems
